          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "perspicuus is built on perspiciō \"to see through\" (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), from per \"through\" and the old verb speciō \"to look\". English perspicuous comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
