              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cōnstantia, cōnstantiae — \"steadiness, firmness, consistency\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Cōnstantiam eius omnēs laudant. Everyone praises his steadiness."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cōnstantia, cōnstantiae f. A person of cōnstantia holds the same view today as yesterday. English constancy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cōnstantia is the noun made from the present participle of a verb built on con- \"together\" and stō \"to stand\" (Lewis & Short): standing firm. English constancy and constant come from the same family."
            }
          ]
        },
